  "definition": "Action Upon Request for Decision Within 30 Days",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "En 1504.02",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1500.html",
  "prefLabel": "En 1504.02 Action Upon Request for Decision Within 30 Days",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1504.02 Action Upon Request for Decision Within 30 Days. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the department shall issue or deny a license within 30 days of receipt of a written request therefor from an applicant made 90 or more days after the filing of an application. The department’s non-receipt of information requested of an applicant shall be a consideration in any decision made pursuant to such a request for a decision within 30 days.",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1500.html"
}
